<PageLayout
  title="About — Tao Jiang"
  description="About Tao Jiang — Statistical Scientist at Genentech/Roche, working on machine learning, bioinformatics, and causal inference."
>
  <h1
    class="mb-6 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 dark:text-white"
  >
    About Me
  </h1>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      I am a Statistical Scientist at <a
        href="https://www.gene.com/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Genentech</a
      >, a member of the Roche group, working on the late phase solid tumor
      (oncology) team. My work focuses on applying statistical and machine
      learning methods to advance clinical research in oncology.
    </p>

    <h2>Research Interests</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Machine Learning</strong> — Variable selection, tree-based
        models, and high-dimensional inference
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Bioinformatics</strong> — Genomics data analysis and
        computational biology
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Causal Inference</strong> — Causal reasoning in observational
        studies and clinical trials
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Education</h2>
    <p>
      I received my PhD in Statistics and Bioinformatics from <a
        href="https://www.ncsu.edu/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">North Carolina State University</a
      >, where I was advised by Dr. <a
        href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=VCbEFscAAAAJ&hl=en"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Alison Motsinger-Reif</a
      >. My dissertation, <a
        href="https://repository.lib.ncsu.edu/bitstream/handle/1840.20/37296/etd.pdf?sequence=1"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
        ><em
          >High Dimensional Linear and Tree-based Models in Bioinformatics</em
        ></a
      >, explored methods for handling high-dimensional data in biological
      applications.
    </p>

    <h2>Publications</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a
          href="https://academic.oup.com/bioinformatics/article/37/7/976/5910548"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          >Knockoff boosted tree for model-free variable selection</a
        > — <em>Bioinformatics</em>, 2020
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      See my full publication list on <a
        href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=NeJg-u4AAAAJ&hl=en&authuser=1"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Google Scholar</a
      >.
    </p>

    <blockquote>
      <p>
        The world always seems brighter when you've just made something that
        wasn't there before.
      </p>
      <cite>— Neil Gaiman</cite>
    </blockquote>
  </div>
